<noinclude>
One system a species exists in, as a row on its page, written by [[Form:Species]] into [[Template:Species]].
It stores the row, and hands it to [[Module:Species]], which lists it in the infobox and sets the categories:
Category:<system> species, the list NPC stat blocks pick from,
and when playable is ticked Category:<system> playable species, the list PC stat blocks pick from.

{{#cargo_declare:_table=Species_systems
|system=String
|playable=Boolean
}}

<templatedata>
{
	"description": "One system a species exists in. Goes inside the in_systems parameter of {{Species}}. Easiest to fill in with the form: Edit with form.",
	"params": {
		"system": {
			"label": "System",
			"description": "A system page, such as E5",
			"type": "wiki-page-name",
			"required": true
		},
		"playable": {
			"label": "Playable species",
			"description": "Yes if a player can pick it in this system",
			"type": "boolean"
		}
	},
	"format": "inline"
}
</templatedata>
</noinclude><includeonly>{{#if:{{{system|}}}|{{#cargo_store:_table=Species_systems
|system={{{system}}}
|playable={{{playable|No}}}
}}{{#invoke:Species|row}}}}</includeonly>
